        "original_id": "52c33b31-8784-53a2-8204-b3989afc4eee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Regency Road, Adelaide; Klemzig; Dudley Park; Croydon\n- Topics: Road route; suburb boundaries; electoral district coverage\n\nFacts:\n- Regency Road in Adelaide is located about 6 km north of the city centre.\n- Regency Road runs from Arndale Shopping Centre in Kilkenny in the west to Broadview in the east.\n- Regency Road continues east as Muller Road and ends at North East Road in Klemzig.\n- Klemzig is a suburb of Adelaide in the City of Port Adelaide Enfield.\n- Dudley Park is bordered on the north by Regency Road, on the south by Simpson Avenue, on the east by the Adelaide-Gawler railway line, and on the west by a line running north-south from the Harrison Road-Simpson Avenue intersection to Regency Road.\n- The electoral district of Croydon includes Dudley Park, Kilkenny, and parts of Ferryden Park.\n- The electoral district of Croydon also includes Allenby Gardens, Beverley, Brompton, Bowden, Croydon, West Croydon, Croydon Park, Devon Park, Flinders Park, Hindmarsh, West Hindmarsh, Renown Park, Ridleyton, Welland, Woodville Gardens, and Woodville Park.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
